# The Node stage runs `npm ci` and then copies frontend/ over the result, so a
# developer's node_modules would land on top of the one just installed. That is
# not merely wasteful: esbuild and rollup ship per-platform binaries, so a
# Windows or macOS tree copied into the alpine stage fails the build outright.
# The same COPY would drop a stale dist/ in, which `vite build` then rebuilds
# anyway. Excluding both also keeps a few hundred megabytes out of the context
# sent to the daemon on every build.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
